"integer"}},"required":["schema","request_id","hecate_source"],"type":"object"},"rules":"Implement the supplied logical graph exactly, including every named output.\\nOnly @hc.func(\\"c,p,...\\") decorated functions: golden plus at most 16 scalar-Expr helpers.\\nGolden parameters must match layout.inputs in order, followed by zero_ct; all are c.\\nEvery physical layout.inputs chunk is encrypted separately and repeated across\\n16384 slots. P=layout.input_slot_period. Different logical tensors never share a chunk.\\nReturn one ciphertext per physical output chunk in ciphertext-index order, with\\nits chunk values in the C-order prefix, repeated every P slots. Other slots are unobserved.\\nArithmetic +,-,*, unary minus requires a ciphertext operand. Public constants are immutable\\nscalar or length-P values in public_constants; finite literals with magnitude<=1024 allowed.\\nPositive rotate(k) reads slot j+k; only positive powers of two below P are callable.\\nCompose rotations for other displacements. Linear is a reduction, not elementwise multiply.\\nzero_ct is client-encrypted zero, not an extra model input or a bootstrap substitute.\\nCompiler owns security, scale, level, rescale, modswitch and relinearization.\\nHelpers have typed scalar c/p positional parameters, no recursion, defaults, kwargs or imports.\\nPublic bounded range loops, assignments, tuple/list unpacking and final returns are permitted.\\nnp.array(data,dtype=object), literal indexing/slicing, reshape/flatten/copy/transpose/T/item\\noperate on whole Expr storage: rank<=4, cells<=16, never ciphertext slots.\\nArray-left +,-,* uses outer-storage broadcasting. Scalar +=,-=,*= rebind; array name-target\\naugmentation mutates shared storage, copies remain independent. No subscript writes.\\nStarred calls expand the first axis into scalar Expr arguments. No encrypted conditions,\\nwhile, arbitrary calls, I/O, network, bootstrap, raw level changes or hidden data access.\\nExpanded work<=4096, golden work<=1024, source<=65536 bytes, AST and sandbox bounds apply.\\nDo not change weights, layout, reference, numerical thresholds or test inputs.\\nReturn only response-schema JSON. Numerical correctness requires real encrypted validation.\\n\\nChunk bindings for unified-capacity-chunked-inputs-v3: logical_inputs declares tensors, inputs binds physical\\nDSL parameters. For each entry, flatten that logical tensor in C order, take\\n[offset:offset+elements], then zero-pad to P. Chunks are encrypted independently.\\nEach named output lists chunks with immutable ciphertext index, offset and elements.\\nReassemble via output_selectors in named-output order. Cross-chunk operations must\\nimplement logical tensor semantics; rotating a chunk alone is not a whole-tensor rotation.\\nIntermediate layouts are candidate choices; immutable input/output bindings cannot change.\\nAt most sixteen model chunks plus zero_ct and sixteen output chunks; existing budgets apply.\\n\\nCapacity ABI unified-capacity-chunked-inputs-v3: resource_profile and physical bindings are immutable.\\nThis request selects the general-tensors-v1 profile (logical rank 1..32). At most sixteen input chunks and sixteen output chunks;\\nappend exactly one trusted encrypted zero_ct to the ordered x0,x1,... entry parameters.\\nLogical tensors retain their declared shapes and names. Flatten each separately in C order,\\npartition into P-element chunks, pad each final chunk, and repeat each chunk across 16384 slots.\\nReturn all physical ciphertexts in the frozen output order; selectors decode only logical elements.\\nEvery logical operation must include all chunks, including tails. A chunk rotation is not a\\nwhole-tensor rotation. Reductions exclude padded slots, including padding changed by public bias.\\nNative helpers retain sixteen parameters and object storage retains sixteen cells.\\nSource, AST, work, sandbox, depth, rotations and security limits remain unchanged.\\nLogical input/output element limits: 4096/4096.\\nIndividual operators retain their registered rank and axis restrictions. Object-array construction bounds remain unchanged.\\nStatic transpose/permute use the tensor_route masks from the frozen packing descriptor; they route logical C-order elements across chunks.\\n\\nPublic packing capacity-public-tensors-v10: bindings name immutable length-P\\nvectors, not extra model parameters. Linear strategies are public layout plans.\\nFor tensor_route and pool_gather with baby_step/giant_step, the registered mask\\nis pre-rotated: mask[j] is the destination coefficient at (j-giant_step) mod P.\\nThe complete route reads input_chunk at the declared step and places its values\\nin output_chunk; shifts spanning chunks use their declared source/destination.\\nspatial_window factors an unpadded average window into flat sums, then selects\\nonly valid spatial anchors. spatial_windows.axes gives each count and flat\\nstride; pool_shift offset is a zero-filled flat displacement before pooling\\ngather, not an independent tensor input. pool_gather includes the average\\ndivisor. Intermediate windows across row/channel boundaries are never selected.\\nThese plans change physical routing only; the declared model mathematics,\\nweights, layouts, resource limits and numerical reference remain fixed.\\n\\nspatial_stream sums a public list of offsets within one source chunk before\\ngathering valid anchors. spatial_streams lists input_chunk and offsets; stream\\nin pool_stream_gather selects that list entry, while input_chunk records the\\noriginal physical input. Gather masks include the average divisor.\\ntiled_row_sum Linear first places independent rows at a power-of-two stride,\\nperforms a row-local weighted sum, selects row starts, then packs output rows.\\nlinear_tiles.method, public row weights and row masks bind this layout.\\n\\nchannel_affine preserves inference BatchNorm: bn_gain and bn_offset are public\\nlength-P vectors derived from the frozen statistics, gain, bias and epsilon.\\nEach output chunk equals input_chunk * bn_gain + bn_offset. Tail positions\\nremain zero and are outside the logical output.\\naligned_suffix sums complete disjoint suffix rows. suffix_windows\\nbinds the row width and count; suffix_gather observes only row starts after\\na width-element rolling sum made from binary rotation/addition windows. Masks include the mean divisor\\nwhen applicable. Unobserved rolling-window positions are not tensor outputs.\\n\\nStatic slice routes preserve C-order tensor indexing: starts, stops and positive\\nsteps are model attributes. tensor_route masks bind each source chunk and output\\nchunk, including zero-filled tails. Removing or inserting singleton dimensions\\nuses reshape after selection and does not rotate ciphertext slots by itself.\\n\\nV10 selects shallower public Linear bindings before estimated arithmetic work,\\nwithin the existing constant registry. planning_costs reports conservative\\nplaintext multiplication depth; compiler_feasibility remains unknown until\\nreal compilation. These costs are neither remaining levels nor a scale proof.\\nFor linear_diagonal, each binding selects input_chunk, output_chunk and step.\\nIts public length-P vector is expressed in destination coordinates: destination\\nlane j receives vector[j] times source input_chunk lane (j+step) mod P. Sum all\\nsuch routes for each output_chunk, then add that chunk\'s linear_bias when present.\\nRotating a source by step uses the allowed power-of-two rotations; a vector is\\nan immutable bound value, not a table to index during encrypted computation.\\nFor aligned_suffix each selected complete row is wholly inside one input chunk;\\nunselected rolling-window positions and padding do not contribute. Binary\\nwindows support non-power-of-two widths using disjoint power-of-two segments.\\nCipher broadcasting may replicate a mask0-isolated source cell to arithmetic\\nruns of destination positions using binary rotation/addition, separately per\\nchunk. This preserves all logical elements and never rotates across chunks.\\n\\nPublic weight descriptor contract v2:\\nLarge public tensors retain shape and content-hash descriptors.\\nmath_roles supplies checked public mathematical values and exact bindings for\\nscalar operands and polynomial coefficients. Other public tensors retain existing\\nconstant_origins block/layout roles and descriptors; no scalar Plain is required\\nfor each tensor element.\\nCoefficient index is the declared ascending degree/basis index. pN numbering\\nhas no mathematical meaning. Use the listed immutable Plain names and retain\\nevery nonzero coefficient. exact_zero denotes mathematical zero, not a request\\nto produce a transparent ciphertext. A zero result requires the existing trusted\\nencrypted-zero capability. Tensor/scalar equality does not change logical shape,\\nlayout, matrix semantics, rotation keys or backend capability. These are public\\nmathematical roles, not a DSL implementation or private numerical answers.\\n\\n","schema":1,"semantic_guidance":{"array_cells":"whole Exprs, never slots","linear":"cross-element weighted reduction","model":"logical tensor graph","packing":"common periodic inputs, named packed outputs","schema":1,"scope":"bounded native construction, no unrestricted Python"},"task":"hecate-unified-graph-synthesis-v1"}'

